A brief overview of key terms:

`%a10e`
    Processor architecture.
`->`
    Then.

(1) INFO ABOUT UTILITY
=======================================================================================================

The build master for x86_64 and aarch64 architectures, both in x86_64 systems and in aarch64 systems. 
It is used for building:
	1)	catpkg (Various contents)

	2)	catpkg-installer-%a10e (catpkg installation master)
	
	3)	catpkg-make-%a10e (Updating the current version or building another architecture)

Launch: 
`./catpkg-make-%a10e`

Permissions to run: Default.

(2) USAGE
=======================================================================================================

	To launch, use `./catpkg-make-%a10e`. You will be prompted to enter a number: “Enter a number:” 
to select an option:
	1)	Building the catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage

	2)	Building catpkg-installer-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X 
	( catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage build is required )
	
	3)	catpkg-make-(aarch64/x86_64) ( Update )

< P.S. About options >
1 - This option creates a package .tmp/catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage,
with the architecture of your choice; the version is automatically taken from build-data/PACKAGEINFO.

2 - This parameter creates the main binary installation 
file catpkg with the option to select the processor architecture; 
the package Building the catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage is used for the build.

3 - Updates or creates a build master with architecture selection.

-> To confirm, press “Enter”.

	Regardless of the selected option, enter the number “Enter a number: ” 
to select the available architectures for the build.

-> To confirm, press “Enter”.

After that, the assembly process will continue.

